#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:9
msgid "What I do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:11
msgid ""
"Teach agents how to use the `hero relevant` command to surface relevant "
"conventions, past work, and in-flight specs when a developer works "
"directly without using `/design` or `/deliver`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:13
msgid "When to use me"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:15
msgid ""
"Load this skill when an agent is about to do implementation work that was"
" not initiated through the spec workflow (no `/design`, no `/deliver`). "
"This applies most often to the `engineer` agent receiving a direct task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:17
msgid "How nudging works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:19
msgid ""
"The `hero relevant` command checks the spec corpus index for context "
"relevant to the files being touched and returns a message calibrated to "
"the team's configured nudge level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:21
msgid "Nudge levels (configured in hero.json)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md
msgid "Level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md
msgid "Behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md
msgid "`off`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md
msgid "No nudge output. Agent works silently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md
msgid "`gentle`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"Short summary: convention names, past spec count, in-flight spec names. "
"One-liner references with a pointer to `hero relevant` for more detail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md
msgid "`assertive`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"Full context block: convention descriptions with paths, past work titles,"
" in-flight spec warnings, and a recommendation to use `/design`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:29
msgid ""
"The level is set in `hero.json` under `team.nudge_level`. Default is "
"`gentle`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:31
msgid "Running the nudge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:33
msgid ""
"Before writing code for a direct task, identify the files you intend to "
"change and run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:35
msgid "hero relevant --files src/api/users.ts src/db/queries/users.sql\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:39
msgid "Interpreting the output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:41
msgid "**If empty** — no relevant context exists. Proceed normally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:42
msgid ""
"**If conventions are listed** — follow them in your implementation, even "
"without a spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:43
msgid ""
"**If past specs are listed** — be aware of prior design decisions. Don't "
"contradict them without reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:44
msgid ""
"**If in-flight specs are listed** — warn the developer that someone else "
"may be working on overlapping files. Suggest coordinating."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:46
msgid "Presenting the nudge to the developer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:48
msgid ""
"Include the nudge output in your response, clearly separated from your "
"implementation work. Do not lecture or moralize. The nudge is a factual "
"summary of what exists in the corpus, not a judgment about how the "
"developer chose to work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:50
msgid "Good:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:51
msgid ""
"## Implementation\n"
"[your code changes]\n"
"\n"
"---\n"
"Hero found relevant context for the files you're touching:\n"
"- Convention: api-response-format\n"
"- 2 past specs touched these files\n"
"- In-flight spec: add-user-search (delivering)\n"
"\n"
"Run `hero relevant --files <paths>` for full details.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:64
msgid "Bad:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:65
msgid "You should have used /design first! Let me show you what you missed...\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:69
msgid "When the developer ignores the nudge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:71
msgid ""
"That's fine. The nudge is advisory. The developer may have good reasons "
"to skip the spec workflow for small, low-risk changes. Do not re-nudge or"
" escalate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:73
msgid "Relationship to context injection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:75
msgid "Nudging is the lightweight complement to context injection:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:77
msgid ""
"**Context injection** (via `hero relevant`) is the full-power version "
"used by delivery leads during `/deliver`. It generates a structured block"
" with conventions, past work, decisions, and known risks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:78
msgid ""
"**Nudging** (via `hero relevant`) is the lightweight version used by "
"agents working directly. It surfaces the same information in a shorter "
"format, appropriate for ad-hoc work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/nudge-awareness/SKILL.md:80
msgid ""
"If a nudge reveals significant context (many conventions, in-flight "
"conflicts), the agent should suggest that the developer consider using "
"`/design` to get full context injection. But this is a suggestion, not a "
"requirement."
msgstr ""

